# [Sizzle Reel](sizzle)

The shot list. Times are in BEATS, not seconds - `sz_play(key, bpm)` multiplies every
`Seconds:` by `60/bpm`, so at 120bpm a beat is half a second and `Seconds: 8` is a
four-second shot. Retiming the whole reel to a different track is one flag.

Every shot uses `Framing:` rather than `Lens:`. Framing is hull-relative, so a shot
reads the same whether it is pointed at a shuttle or a starbase, and moving a spawn
in `sz_stage.mast` does not silently rebreak it.

`Subject:` names a CAST that `sz_stage.mast` binds before playing - which is why there
is not one coordinate in this file.

